{"trans": "Promote fair competition, oppose deception and rivalry, and encourage a flourishing and diverse online environment; advocate unity and collaboration, reject harming others for self-interest, and foster mutual benefits and shared success on the internet."}
{"trans": "In summary, perhaps more overseas companies believe that listing in the United States is more trouble than it's worth, prompting them to opt for a strategic exit. However, this by no means indicates that they are prepared to abandon the American market."}
{"trans": "He believes that in such a jittery market environment, it is increasingly difficult for gold to remain unscathed, and talking about breaking the $1,000 barrier is likely another pipe dream."}
{"trans": "The police officer explained that the students' actions were an act of bravery, as they stepped forward without hesitation during the elderly person's critical moment of falling into the water, which is quite admirable. It is understood that the elderly person has a mild mental illness and, after receiving full medical treatment at the hospital, has been stabilized and is out of danger."}
{"trans": "Of course, the methods mentioned above are only a few limited yet effective approaches for review. The arrangements for the final sprint of preparation should be diverse and varied, and they should also be tailored to the unique characteristics of each examinee. Wishing all candidates an immediate success and a triumphant victory!"}
{"trans": "Formed another long river of this life and present era  \nAt the place where Zhaojun dismounted her horse,  \nRiding on the stones of history, they still speak.  \nThe grass is as green as that year, flowers carry the fragrance of the past.  \nA herd of cattle and sheep do not recognize today,  \nBowing their heads, humble and cautious.  \nIn the meticulous flow of time, drinking water and thinking of the source.  \nPeople sit amidst the aroma of wine,  \nThe autumn waters of South Lake, the night air free of mist."}
{"trans": "This belief is not about seeking a life of constant indulgence, nor is it about pursuing longevity. Since one cannot live twice, how can one realize the meaning and value of life before death? Even if shattered to pieces, one should leave behind a resonant echo like jade striking the ground with a metallic ring, and burst forth with the brilliance of life in this world."}
{"trans": "While the others managed to stay calm, drawing their guns and surveying the surroundings for enemy movements, Li Wenbin alone was thrown into a panic. He scrambled headfirst into a clump of grass, his rear end sticking up high and his hands shielding his head, cutting a sorry figure. His companions couldn't help but cover their faces and chuckle, causing Li Wenbin's authority to plummet instantly."}
{"trans": "\"How do you plan to be king?\" the animals asked with a mix of belief and doubt. \"First, mediate disputes impartially and fairly. Second, handle state affairs diligently and without complaint. Third, face strong enemies by leading the charge and fighting at the front. That is my governance speech.\""}
{"trans": "Worldly-wise and well-versed in the vicissitudes of life, he pivoted with the ease of a compass needle—his polestar ever-shifting, never fixed. Blessed with a silver tongue that artfully pleased, he remained unscathed by his own vileness; moreover, his eloquence flowed in an unending stream, unless, of course, the payment fell short."}
{"trans": "The first time I followed my colleagues to the stock exchange, it felt destined that I would form an inseparable bond with stocks. Seventeen springs, summers, autumns, and winters have allowed me to fully experience the ups and downs of the stock market. Through numerous rises and falls, I have become a seasoned veteran, and past events are still vivid in my mind! First, the sea of suffering has no bounds; repent and the shore is at hand."}
{"trans": "The defeated general, after fleeing for a long time, finally came to a halt. He looked up to the sky and sighed: \"I began leading troops at the age of twenty-five, undefeated in every battle and successful in every siege. Now, in my twilight years, I have suffered such a devastating defeat—it absolutely enrages me!\" News of the victory in the defense of Ningyuan reached the imperial court, and everyone, from top to bottom, was overjoyed. They raised their glasses in celebration."}
{"trans": "Newlyweds are greeted by a continuous stream of relatives and friends coming to offer blessings. Therefore, the living room decor should not be overly unconventional but rather prioritize comfort and warmth, ensuring both the hosts feel at ease and guests experience a sense of home. Plush fabric sofas and cushions are indispensable elements."}
{"trans": "I said, let's not extrapolate too much, better stick to the matter at hand. My son said, over the years, I've observed your attitude with a critical eye and feel you treat computers as too sacred. This shouldn’t be touched, that shouldn't be moved. The biggest mental block for you mothers when it comes to learning is treating computers like some kind of deity."}
{"trans": "Always walking on eggshells, afraid of saying the wrong thing, doing the wrong thing, or offending others. The seventh precept: grief—unfortunate events from a lifetime often surface before the eyes, and sadness arises involuntarily. The eighth precept: suspicion—those who are paranoid always think others are plotting against them, so every word and action must be guarded, leading to restlessness and frequent insomnia."}
{"trans": "In another corner was that despicable guillotine: the very disgrace of France, and prone to hide its diminished head—as well it might, doing its work so ill, and so treacherously—which seemed to be alarmed, lest it should be put to shame, and to shrink and cower from the light. Without shedding one drop of precious blood in extenuation of its crimes, and without one humane provision for the soothing of the sufferer, it must ever be enough."}
{"trans": "At this point, the true charm of fighting lies in the vigilant anticipation after arranging a fight, the tense standoff before the fight, the sharp verbal exchanges during mediation, the clinking of glasses after dispersing, the unwavering loyalty when meeting again in the future, and the shoulder-to-shoulder combat in the next fight. This cycle repeats, and the ranks of pacifism continue to grow."}
{"trans": "The baron's such brazen insults are utterly unbearable; just wait, you shameless madman, for the sake of honor, I shall take on the responsibility of revenge. Such brazen insults from everyone, only he can bear the duty of vengeance; even at the cost of his life, he cannot swallow the humiliation."}
{"trans": "It doesn't look like there will be an argument or a storm; everything has already calmed down. But yet again, my mother chose an inopportune moment to ask, \"Would you like to see what I looked like when I was your age?\" My daughter’s reply was odd and equally ill-timed, \"Maybe later, dear mother, some other time.\""}
{"trans": "In dealing with the world, he is still at a beginner's stage, but when it comes to knowledge, he has full confidence. However eloquent the director may be, he is hardly more tricky and eccentric than the professors at a master's thesis defense. If you ask a woodcutter how to eat a Western meal, he might be at a loss, but if you ask how to chop wood, isn't that second nature to him?!"}
{"trans": "\"You will soon face the consequences of idleness.\" After saying this, the plow ox lowered its head back under the yoke and pulled its cart loaded with manure away. You should live an upright life, always be mindful throughout your years, and guard against laziness and idleness. If you still feel no shame about it, you will inevitably reap what you sow."}
{"trans": "Draw it, and draw it so vividly and true to life. His art repeatedly deceived the eyes of people; at first glance, it was mistaken for real objects, and it was hard to believe they were merely paintings. For centuries, the art of painting had remained lowbrow, unworthy of refined settings, but in his hands, it was revitalized and elevated once again."}
{"trans": "Throughout history, emperors have often been mythologized by people, to the point of being considered sacred and inviolable, mysterious and elusive, thus worshipped and regarded as celestial beings, hence the title \"Son of Heaven.\" In reality, emperors are also human; they can be good or bad. Among them, there are wise rulers with great talent and vision who bring stability and prosperity to the nation, as well as incompetent and foolish monarchs."}
{"trans": "Once upon a time, he \"went out laughing, his face lifted to the sky,\" chanting proudly, \"How could I be a man trapped among mediocrities?\" The deceit and hypocrisy of the officialdom, the sanctimoniousness of the mundane world, and the harsh reality cooled his fervent passion. How could the golden pretense of being a \"court-appointed scholar\" ever cage his untamed heart? In the end, after enduring the frustrations and pains of his political career, he found peace within himself."}
{"trans": "\"For quite some time, a suspicious-looking vagrant has been harassing our territory, stirring up trouble and sowing discord. You are to apprehend this troublemaker by tomorrow and carry out a death sentence.\" \"It will be done as you command, sir,\" the police officers said before departing. The villain, who was one-eyed, did not notice their exchanged winks as they responded."}
{"trans": "Americans have never treated their national leaders as deities, nor do they follow their commands without question. However, Obama yielded to the expectations his supporters had for him. He also believed he was the long-awaited savior they had been waiting for. The silence of the people served as a sobering blow to him. Yet, the sensation of suddenly rising to great heights was so intoxicating that it nearly made him lose his sense of reality."}
{"trans": "The usually amiable Taurus man, pragmatic to the core, finds betrayal from within most intolerable. Do not attempt to probe his true feelings; the steady bull is content with grazing and smiles upon you, much like Jesus watching over his sheep. If you wish to avoid dragging the scene to a Spanish bullring, witnessing rivers of blood and a field littered with casualties, never provoke his jealousy."}
{"trans": "What fun would life be for a Gemini without a little trickery and cleverness? Though they may seem careless and nonchalant usually, once the situation becomes complex, they will strike you by surprise; while everyone else is fighting tooth and nail, they can sit back and reap the spoils. Yet, once they successfully capture everyone’s attention, they turn into carefree princes, walking away elegantly and playing the game of playing hard to get."}
{"trans": "But in reality, as part of the Eurozone and tied to the euro, it is fundamentally an impossibility for Germans to remain unaffected. Initially, the establishment of the Eurozone was driven by the grand vision of shared prosperity. Now, the Greek debt crisis has triggered a European debt crisis, making it natural that the downfall of one affects all. When the city gate catches fire, it harms the fish in the moat; especially when the surrounding areas are already engulfed in flames, with some places nearly reduced to scorched earth."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, direct investment in commodities might be the most straightforward and effective way to hedge against inflation. However, when it comes to commodity investment, people often recall some alarming stories first—those who lost everything speculating on commodity futures or airlines suffering massive losses from crude oil hedging, among others. It seems as though the risks of commodity investment are so high that ordinary investors are deterred from engaging in it."}
{"trans": "The vast sky tolerates the raging of lightning and thunder, thus achieving calm and sunny days; the expansive sea tolerates the fury of violent waves, thus achieving gentle ripples; the silent forest tolerates the cruelty of the survival of the fittest, thus achieving birdsong and floral fragrance. It is because the sky, sea, and forest understand tolerance, know when to yield, and lower themselves to accept, that they attain beauty and uniqueness. Lowering oneself broadens the world."}
{"trans": "Looking at the ever-changing landscape of recent college entrance exams, what we need is a firm grasp of the new trends and directions in exam questions, proactive planning, and a shift from vague perceptions to clear insights. This will enable you to face the challenge with confidence, as if commanding a formidable army, and effortlessly triumph over difficulties. With guidance from expert teachers, turning iron into gold; a journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step; and a towering structure rises from accumulated earth—these principles will help you successfully take the first step in your exam preparation journey!"}
{"trans": "Learning to appreciate oneself is akin to possessing a golden key to happiness. Appreciating oneself does not mean indulging in self-admiration, nor does it imply arrogance or self-obsession, and it certainly is not about being complacent or stagnant. Giving oneself confidence, a dash of joy, and a smile can ensure that happiness in life is never far away. One should often celebrate life on their own terms and learn to seek out a cheerful state of mind."}
{"trans": "Perhaps people are gradually realizing that the internet and traditional industries are not mortal enemies locked in a life-or-death struggle, but rather a perfect pair that can complement each other beautifully. The retail sector is increasingly showing characteristics of channel integration, with online and offline channels penetrating and combining more deeply. Currently, Taobao has opened physical stores, while traditional businesses are venturing into the internet in droves. Examples range from Gome and Suning Appliances to Walmart and Carrefour supermarkets, among countless others."}
{"trans": "In summary, uncertainties in the commodity market continue to emerge, financial hegemony still manipulates the market, and the rules of the game change frequently. Against the backdrop of both optimism and concern over the global debt crisis and world economic recovery, the US dollar remains the primary factor influencing commodity trends. European and American economic policies follow closely, while domestic regulations add fuel to the fire. The interplay of these three factors in terms of capital flows and market confidence is bound to cause significant volatility in the commodity market."}
{"trans": "Chinese red is an intriguing spiritual culture, a unique ethos of the Chinese people. It represents a powerful force—unyielding perseverance, sincere dedication, hard work, kindness, and resilience, embodying the millennia-old Chinese qualities of noble spirit and grandeur. As a leading furniture company, Liantianhong passionately conveys the flame of Chinese red. Guided by a business philosophy rooted in integrity, it pioneered transparent workshop production, setting an industry benchmark and revitalizing the landscape of the furniture sector."}
{"trans": "Physical Characteristics: In *Journey to the West*, Tang Sanzang is depicted as tall in stature, with elegant manners and a gentle, benevolent nature, possessing profound knowledge in Buddhist teachings. He endured eighty-one hardships on his pilgrimage to the West to retrieve sacred scriptures, yet his devotion never wavered. With the assistance of Sun Wukong, Zhu Bajie, and Sha Heshang, he overcame numerous difficulties and finally succeeded in obtaining the true scriptures. Sun Wukong, also known as the Monkey King and disciple named Pilgrim, is Tang Sanzang's first disciple. He has piercing golden eyes, can transform into seventy-two different forms, and ride on clouds and mist. He detests evil as if it were his enemy, fears no hardship, and is characterized by his perseverance, bravery, and fearlessness."}
{"trans": "3. Approach to Learning: I have my own set of methods—\"developing a sense for problems\" and \"avoiding late nights.\" In fact, once learning becomes second nature through practice, while it may not be effortless, one can still have a clear grasp of things. I do not advocate for the tactic of excessive drilling, as there is no need to repeatedly tackle similar problems. Instead, we should compare and reflect on analogous questions, summarizing the methods to solve them. The so-called \"sense for problems\" is similar to what we often refer to as a \"feel for the language\" in English."}
{"trans": "The Great Wall of China, the world's longest man-made structure, stretches majestically across the peaks of northern China's rugged mountains, spanning over 6,700 kilometers. Initially constructed during the Spring and Autumn and Warring States periods, it is a rare ancient military defense project in the history of human architecture. Renowned for its long history, immense scale, and magnificent presence, it has been inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List and is celebrated as the \"Eighth Wonder of the World.\""}
{"trans": "With capital, they remain low-key; being extraordinary and refusing to be vulgar, they choose to stay understated. Essentially, luxury goods are exceptional, even unique. They do not tolerate any compromise in quality or their embodiment of fashion, and they possess impeccable superiority in artistic culture and style culture. Luxury goods are by no means necessities of life, but their unparalleled craftsmanship and profound brand heritage undoubtedly make them essentials in life."}
{"trans": "Although her legs felt as though they were filled with lead, she still strode briskly across the street toward the parking garage. Now, drowsy and driving alone on the fluorescent-lit concrete lane, she felt her consciousness blurring. When she had parked here seventeen hours earlier, two vans had been parked on either side, so close that she had to squeeze out of her car awkwardly. Now her beat-up \"Taurus\" sat like an orphan, solitary on the eighth level of the parking area."}
{"trans": "A decade ago, perhaps no one knew that the internet could move with laptops, just as twenty years ago, people could hardly imagine that phones would fit in pockets and become ever-present companions in the work and daily lives of modern society. Today, a variety of smart terminals are radiating unprecedented magic, subtly reshaping human lifestyles. In the next ten years, there is a high likelihood of groundbreaking innovations emerging in fields such as terminals, displays, virtual reality, information sharing, and consumer electronics."}
{"trans": "We advocate for team spirit and revere the heroism of risking one's life to save a comrade. However, we must ensure that we do not become a burden to our comrades and avoid putting them at unnecessary risk for our rescue. Strict training and the ability to make quick decisions in the field are absolutely essential! Until you have experienced the heat of battle, refrain from playing your armchair general games in front of us. Some things are beyond the understanding of a freshly graduated student officer like you!"}
{"trans": "It is my fault for not deeply grasping the five-character poem about the poplar tree or my grandfather's seven-character verse. Although I have made some progress through daily accumulation in the art of \"playing dumb,\" I have yet to attain true enlightenment. Last night, a mute mosquito bit my neck, and I cried out loudly, \"How dare you bite without making a sound? How dare you suck blood without being open and honorable? Why not learn to be an upright mosquito, charging straight at my neck with a roar?\" Thus, I live wearily and absurdly, often hearing the mocking hum of mosquitoes."}
{"trans": "As barbecue joints sprout up like mushrooms in every corner of the city, people's nights are becoming increasingly flavorful. However, it is truly difficult to enjoy both delicious food and an elegant environment. As the setting sun dyes the sky red, blending with the lush green of the pitch, tables are arranged gracefully across the terrain. The grill masters skillfully tend to the flames, waitstaff weave through the crowd, and customers chat and laugh, thoroughly enjoying the relaxed atmosphere. Soothing music fills the air, adding a touch of charm to the scene."}
{"trans": "Hearing this, the old man let out a long sigh and said, \"Ah, I've narrowly escaped death more than once—it's truly a long story!\" And so, this proud and stubborn old man finally opened up to me, a writer he had never met before, sharing the hardships of his life and the depths of his inner world for the very first time... As he spoke, at times impassioned, at times heavy-hearted, at times with tears streaming down his aged face, and at other times bursting into hearty laughter, I felt the tumultuous and tragic life of a seventy-year-old man who had weathered countless storms, as well as the irresistible twists of fate..."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, the political arena in the West is far from being as clean as people imagine. Beneath the veneer of integrity flows murky waters, albeit with a uniquely Western flavor. On the surface, politicians grandly \"sow seeds,\" while behind the scenes, they legally \"reap the harvest.\" Seasoned politicians and shrewd capitalists collaborate seamlessly and tacitly, mastering the art of mutual back-scratching and power-for-money exchanges to such an extent that it is done openly and lawfully—so skillfully that even Western democracy and legal systems are powerless against it."}
{"trans": "After wading for several hours, a vast, suddenly expansive cavern leaped into view. \"Oh my, this is no mere cave, it's practically an underground forest,\" a team member exclaimed. The cavern was as large as a basketball court, with its ground strewn with rugged rocks, murmuring streams, and crisscrossing gullies. Stone pillars as thick as bowls grew over ten meters high, alongside massive stone curtains, uneven stone drapes, and intricately intertwined stalactites... all in bizarre shapes, resembling a primeval forest. Adding to this, a multitude of crystals sparkled under the light, making anyone walking among them feel as if they had stepped into a fairytale world."}
{"trans": "The heart can also shrink to a minuscule size, able to hold only a home, one person, a sesame seed, or a drop of virus. A hint of rain can drown it; a wisp of wind can shatter it. A single rumor can plunge it into unbearable pain; one conspiracy can doom it irrevocably. The heart can be as hard as any metal known to mankind. It can be incredibly soft, weeping softly like silk or satin. It can be resilient, enduring countless injuries and grievances yet remaining as smooth as ever. It can also be fragile, shattering instantly at the slightest misstep."}
{"trans": "Strolling through, one sees shaded woods and blooming flowers vying in beauty, serene and tranquil beyond compare. The gentle breeze carries a delicate fragrance, instantly refreshing the heart and mind. The winding stone paths lead to secluded spots, the well-arranged flowers and trees flourish gracefully, and the crisp, melodious sound of flowing water weaves together multiple layers of scenery, forming a vivid and vibrant picture of life. With every step, the view changes—each flower, leaf, grass, tree, stone, and spring exudes a unique charm, allowing one to escape the worldly hustle and experience the beauty of harmony with nature and spiritual purification. Lingering in such scenery, one fully savors the joy of earthly pleasures."}
{"trans": "The furious former whaling ship said, \"This is the whale we caught.\" The smug current whaling ship said, \"Then how did it end up here?\" The furious side said, \"It escaped again.\" The smug side said, \"You should have tied it up properly.\" The furious side said,"}
{"trans": "Your sanctimonious appearance cannot conceal your arrogance and greed! Pretentious doctors, babbling witches, and smooth-tongued frauds mock our incompetence—beware the slap! You, ungrateful husbands, who think yourselves clever and capable, belittle love and kindness."}
{"trans": "A farce that lasted for two months has come to an end, and it's unclear why Foxconn was so enraged by these two reports. A wealthy corporation is never short of think tanks. Crisis management tactics can range from tearful pleas to loud displays of anger: perhaps to make an example out of someone or to create a diversion."}
{"trans": "To award according to merits, the most delicious food rightfully belongs to it. \"I see you as pitiable and laughable, so arrogant and conceited,\" replied the wild duck. \"Your viewpoint is biased. We wild ducks fly to the ends of the earth, free from all worries, making the whole world our home. But you depend on others for a living; we rely on our own efforts, while you beg for food from others.\""}
{"trans": "The beginning of an article is the most difficult part. It must be striking and vigorous, straightforward, and sharp to captivate the reader. There is no need to beat around the bush or use clichés. He also told me that when reasoning reaches a point of complexity, a metaphor can resolve all entangled arguments effortlessly—how economical, how skillful! Such insights, among others."}
{"trans": "She began to divine with great seriousness. After bustling about for a while, she put on a show of examining the sand tray and making calculations before raising her head to look at Kudir and saying, \"You damned shameless scoundrel! How dare you talk nonsense in front of me! The divination clearly shows that you are Kudir, a bandit who kills and plunders, commits every evil imaginable, and is guilty of unpardonable crimes.\""}
{"trans": "The castle truly was like a paradise. He couldn't help but feel captivated by the sight of the magnificent structure, filled with a mix of astonishment and envy. As they strolled through the garden, they picked and ate fresh fruits, immersing themselves in the atmosphere filled with birdsong and floral fragrance, making them reluctant to leave. By the time they had leisurely explored the entire castle, it was already dark. They returned to the great hall by the pond, intending to spend the night there."}
{"trans": "The air conditioning is indeed effective. The cool, fresh air, the well-organized layout, the well-dressed guests, and the polite waitstaff—all of these elements make the place feel like a hidden paradise, exceptionally comfortable. But what spoils the atmosphere are always the people. Those impeccably dressed gentlemen are all eating with greasy, gleaming faces, which makes one feel quite uncomfortable. They all nod in greeting to Nikolai, and for some reason, a few even wink at him."}
{"trans": "The Japanese began to waver. Watching their hopeless situation and inevitable defeat, they finally abandoned their resistance and fled into the city. The armored trains continued to sweep back and forth, mopping up the remaining enemy forces—truly resembling two mighty land dragons advancing triumphantly, crushing everything in their unstoppable path. They flattened the enemy’s entrenched bunkers and fortifications and sent slower-moving opponents to their doom. These trains were a stirring declaration of victory for the Chinese army, proclaiming the imminent end of the stubborn invaders."}
{"trans": "After this calamity, our family never recovered its former prosperity. The family fortune declined, and we struggled in poverty and hardship, barely surviving the pangs of hunger and cold. The old locust tree, too, lost its former splendor. The remaining stump stood solitary and alone, desolate in the half-barren courtyard, enduring the wind and rain, exposed to the chill of dew and frost. For many years, it remained listless, neither sprouting nor branching, and utterly neglected. It could only stand stiffly there, as if \"sighing up to the sky.\""}
{"trans": "All reactionary things will not fall unless you strike them. As a rule, where the broom does not reach, the dust will not vanish of itself. You are all doomed, only I, Zhang Pujing, a loyal Bolshevik, upright and honest, wavering and hesitant, flat on my back, prostrate in admiration, everything going smoothly, the Marco Polo Bridge Incident, the Eight Immortals crossing the sea, the vast land of China, perfect in every way. Haha, revolution is not a dinner party, not writing an essay, not painting a picture, not doing embroidery; it cannot be so refined, so leisurely and gentle, so temperate, kind, courteous, restrained and magnanimous. The proletariat has placed all you freaks and monsters under dictatorship."}
{"trans": "Excessive admiration for top scorers in the college entrance examination may lead them to feel superior. Some develop a sense of complacency, arrogance, and self-importance, unconsciously relaxing their demands on themselves in future work and life, becoming stagnant and struggling to cooperate with others. Others may believe they must never fall short of others in any situation, excessively pursuing perfection, acting overly cautious, indecisive, and rigidly adhering to rules. These tendencies can cause former top scorers to lack creativity and passion in their endeavors, ultimately hindering their ability to achieve great success."}
{"trans": "I will treat every patient equally, whether they are dressed in luxury or rags, whether they are handsome or plain, whether they are wealthy or in hardship, whether their status is noble or humble, whether they are pristine or scarred, whether they suffer from complex conditions or minor ailments, whether they are courteous or rude to me, whether they are refined or uneducated, whether they are humorous or dull, whether they are dignitaries or ordinary citizens..."}
{"trans": "Love is free. That involuntary admiration, that unstoppable longing, that deep affection of sharing hardships, and that devoted love of mutual support are the most profound comfort and the strongest reliance in life. All of this is free, and cannot be bought with money. Goals are free. Whether a prince in fine robes or a homeless child in tattered clothes, as long as one is willing, they can set a goal for their life. This goal can be grand or ordinary, splendid or simple—as long as you wish, you can have it."}
{"trans": "Once you have set your own goal, you should focus your energy, plan the path to success, and then move forward with full effort. During this time, you must not be half-hearted, distracted, or easily swayed by new temptations. In this process, you must strictly eliminate doubt and fear, as they will undermine your fighting spirit, disrupt your forward momentum, and hinder your efforts to achieve your goal with full commitment. Those filled with doubt and fear will ultimately achieve nothing and possess nothing. When doubt and fear creep into your mind, your goals, energy, motivation, and all resolute thoughts will be severely shaken and crumble."}
{"trans": "A cultivated person holds deep reverence and respect for the noble qualities of humanity, such as loyalty, courage, trustworthiness, diligence, mutual aid, self-sacrifice, fearlessness in the face of danger, endurance of hardship, and unwavering perseverance. Not everyone may be able to practice these virtues, but they understand how to admire and celebrate them. It is acceptable for a person to be timid or lazy, but they should not disguise these flaws as noble traits. Nor should they slander those who achieve such virtues as hypocrites simply because they themselves cannot attain them. You may kneel in the mud, but you must not smear that mud upon the chest of the entire world and then solemnly declare that filth is everywhere."}
{"trans": "In this world, there are beginnings that are silent, explosive, cautious, bold, secretive, reluctant, scheming, and honorable. Every journey in life and every task we undertake can be initiated in different ways by different individuals. These approaches reflect a person's temperament, vision, courage, magnanimity, and breadth of mind in navigating life."}
{"trans": "Generally speaking, the final stage of review plays a crucial role in enhancing the overall test preparation process, much like adding the finishing touch to a masterpiece. Therefore, we must attach great importance to this phase, avoiding any mistakes that could render previous efforts futile and cause us to miss out on success. Below, several common pitfalls are explained."}
{"trans": "Currently, the market lacks leadership, major sectors are undergoing adjustments in rotation, and support efforts are weak. Mainstream funds face significant operational challenges, making the overall market very fragile and skittish. At the slightest hint of negative news, panic sets in, leading to intensified selling pressure. Meanwhile, external funds remain on the sidelines, and with the holiday approaching, there is little enthusiasm for bullish positions, further dispersing market sentiment."}
{"trans": "The stubbornly resisting Japanese troops were already on their last legs; their barely held frontline, like a battleship riddled with holes and leaking on all sides, shattered like weathered rock under this fatal blow. In truth, stopping the armored train was not difficult—it only required dismantling the tracks in advance."}
{"trans": "Passing off fish eyes as pearls: how to distinguish the genuine from the fake? Wenwan walnuts are increasingly recognized and cherished by more people, with market prices soaring, and counterfeit products made using high-tech methods are also rampant. Old Hu initially made mistakes too, but now, having seen much of the world, he even sleeps with walnuts in his hands at night, and there is basically nothing that can deceive him anymore. He shared a few tricks for identifying authenticity with the readers of the Evening News."}
{"trans": "Throughout my life, much like others, I have traversed broad highways and crossed narrow, single-plank bridges. I have journeyed along a path marked by bumps, twists, and turns. I must admit I have been quite fortunate, as the successes I achieved and the unwarranted fame I garnered seem somewhat undeserved. On the other hand, my misfortunes were also beyond what ordinary people might endure. During the shocking so-called \"Great Cultural Revolution,\" because I dared to speak out for justice, I nearly lost my life. The physical suffering I endured is something I will never forget."}
{"trans": "Zhuge Liang can be considered one of the greatest military strategists in Chinese history. Comparing himself to Guan Zhong while residing in Longzhong—what immense confidence! How remarkably accurate was his prediction of the tripartite division of the realm! Fresh out of his thatched cottage, he faced Xiahou Dun’s hundred-thousand-strong army without fear; the fire at Bowang Slope won the heartfelt admiration of Guan Yu and Zhang Fei; the blaze at Xinye shattered Cao Ren’s courage; his ingenious strategies in the brocade bags outwitted Zhou Yu three times, showcasing not only his brilliance but also his humor; his unwavering loyalty kept him from claiming the throne, even with Liu Bei’s explicit permission; and his calmness in employing the Empty Fort Strategy out of necessity due to a misjudgment commands nothing but admiration. Yet, what moves me most is not any of these feats, but rather the \"Autumn Wind at Wuzhang Plains.\""}
{"trans": "As night falls upon the mountain village, we hear bursts of sharp dog barking rising and falling one after another. After midnight, the barks fade to barely audible, and lights in the windows flicker on one by one, like the pale faces of cabbage hearts... The moonlight also washes its face by the water pipe in the courtyard..."}
{"trans": "A close-range shot flew wide; a header in front of the goal inexplicably missed; even one-on-one opportunities were squandered... With limited playing time in domestic leagues, the national youth team's ability to capitalize on chances in the attacking third is lamentable, marking the squad's biggest weakness at present."}
{"trans": "However, in a sociological sense, today's Israelis and Palestinians are irreconcilable enemies. This stems both from their estrangement, indifference, suspicion, and hostility after the Jews were exiled from Palestine in 556 BCE, scattering across the world and separating the two peoples for over a millennium, and from the Jews' return to Palestine two thousand years later to establish the state of Israel. Consequently, mutual strife escalated into brutal conflict, erasing all remnants of brotherly affection."}
{"trans": "National policies have been implemented from above, and the industry situation has taken a sharp downturn. The ceramic production areas, being the first to bear the brunt, are struggling like cornered beasts. As enterprises seek ways out, the chilling impact, while bringing shocks and hardships to these regions, has also made them more clearly aware of the path ahead. For detailed reading: With the industry taking a sharp downturn, ceramic production areas are struggling like trapped animals."}
{"trans": "Entering Suzhou's gardens and strolling through its courtyards, one may encounter small bridges over flowing streams, white walls with black tiles, winding paths leading to secluded spots, and ever-changing views with each step. The most profound impression is that its meticulous and rigorous garden-building process shares the same artistic conception as the imperial gardens of the Forbidden City. The arrangement of corridors, pavilions, and waterside lofts unfolds in layers, creating a harmonious and orderly progression. Walking along a 20-meter path evokes the sensation of traversing three to five miles, instantly giving the feeling of wandering within a painting."}
{"trans": "The battlefield situation is ever-changing, and there has never been a fixed formula for achieving victory since ancient times. Matters such as troop deployment and command, whether to attack or defend, engage in positional warfare or mobile warfare, voluntarily abandon positions or hold fast to cities, which areas to relinquish and which to defend—all these should be decided by the frontline commanders themselves, with minimal interference from the high command. In fact, any strategy or tactic can be flexibly applied and integrated; it is hard to say which method is inherently superior. As the saying goes, \"All roads lead to Rome,\" and the ultimate measure of success is victory itself."}
{"trans": "Fiction is the backlight of the soul; you infuse a part of your soul into the work, giving it your flesh and blood, thus achieving artistic depth. This involves two issues: first, writers need to examine the true state of their own souls and shape themselves first; second, the power of sincerity is immense—its significance here lies not only in overcorrecting but also in rejecting a creative climate of affectation, sycophancy, sensationalism, and opportunism. Do not scratch an itch from outside the boot, do not take off your pants to fart, and do not peddle sincerity as a cheap cure-all. I believe sincerity should be a way of life, especially for writers."}
{"trans": "The weathered locust tree before the window,  \nAnd the moon hanging motionless on its motionless boughs like a bell—  \nYet so distant from the sound of bells.  \n\nI know, anything trivial cannot be expected to strike with a golden ring,  \nYet it is precisely these moonlight specks like dust  \nThat make the silent midnight even more like a sunken ship in stillness."}
{"trans": "Ruthless and cruel, cunning and sinister, yet I am kind-hearted, benevolent, and devoted to aiding all beings. In the gloomy Dis Mansion, my soul was intently drawing talismans and inscriptions when suddenly, the mournful voice of Dulcinea del Toboso reached me, revealing that she had fallen victim to an evil enchantment."}
{"trans": "Internet analyst Xu Dandan expressed suspicions that Alibaba has a tendency to \"burn the bridge after crossing the river.\" He stated, \"Capital has its own nature, and it is only natural for them to consider the interests of their shareholders. Accepting investment means accepting the capital agreement. You cannot treat them as gods when you need them and denounce them as demons when they get in the way.\""}
{"trans": "They were astonished by the emperor’s keen eyesight, and although dazzled, they dared not look directly at the throne. We hail from the East, yet the trouble lies afar in the West; Our troops are vast and endless—stretching farther than the eye can see. Wave upon wave they come, each vying to take the lead, their courage bursting forth. Spears in hand, each soldier fights like ten, and every ten like a hundred foes. Countless lives have vanished without a trace."}
{"trans": "He had successfully seized Zubaida and was beside himself with joy when an urgent matter called him away on a long journey. Upon his return, he learned from his family that Zubaida, along with a bag of gold and silver, had vanished without a trace. Enraged by this news, he flew into a furious rage, gnashing his teeth, glaring fiercely, and even beating and cursing himself. He tore his clothes in frustration, growing angrier at the thought of having ended up with nothing."}
{"trans": "2008 was an extraordinary year. On the battlefield of corporate public relations and marketing domestically, it could be described as a storm of blood and wind. For corporate marketing and PR personnel, it seemed as if \"PR crises\" had surged overnight like a fierce beast, striking fear into their hearts. Time raced forward, and in the blink of an eye, we were about to step into 2009. Looking back on the year, perhaps many business owners still feel lingering fear and tread as if on thin ice."}
{"trans": "Leo friends are almost never ones to refuse requests at work; as long as they can showcase their talents and abilities, they will grit their teeth and help out. However, this naturally makes them prone to forgetting details and accumulating a considerable workload. Thus, keeping a handy calendar and weekly schedule is the most suitable office luck enhancer for them. Especially those with a lively and playful style, which perfectly matches their childlike nature, allowing them to tackle tasks with ease even when swamped."}
{"trans": "An excellent essay should feature six or seven types of refined sentences: first, vivid and beautiful metaphorical sentences; second, majestic parallel sentences; third, emotionally rich personified sentences; fourth, culturally profound adapted sentences; fifth, enlightening philosophical sentences; sixth, mutually reinforcing comparative sentences; seventh, elegantly poetic sentences. Skillful use of these refined sentences makes the writing concise yet profound, adds the finishing touch, illuminates the entire piece, achieves multifaceted effects with minimal words, and naturally enhances the literary quality."}
{"trans": "Even more laughable is that Western countries, still grappling with economic woes, are now eager to crank up their money-printing machines despite empty coffers, yet again looking to China to \"feed\" the world... All eyes are now on China, the world’s second-largest economy. If the U.S.-dominated post-Cold War global order is on its last legs, will this emerging economic superpower step up? Or will it let the West reap what it has sown? This time, however, China may be willing but unable to act."}
{"trans": "Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, reigned for fifty-four years, during which he expanded the territory extensively, forming a vast empire that stretched from Liaodong and central Korea in the east, to the shores of Lake Balkhash in the west, deep into central Vietnam in the south, and up to the Sayan Mountains in Outer Mongolia in the north. Under his rule, the population reached nearly sixty million. Objectively speaking, among the hundreds of emperors in Chinese history, very few could match Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, in terms of territorial expansion. Others were considered fortunate if they managed to maintain the inherited realm without becoming disgraced traitors who forfeited sovereignty and humiliated the nation. In this sense alone, Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, can rightly be regarded as an emperor of great talent and bold vision."}
{"trans": "His short stories often reflect the trivialities of ordinary life, lacking dramatic twists and turns, yet they offer a refreshing experience due to their unique perspectives and undeniable personal inclinations. He excels at creating distinctive, individualized characters, which is precisely the hallmark of a gifted writer."}
{"trans": "Some people boast and bluff, flaunting their authority and influence, often claiming to be the industry leader or the first of its kind to seek selling points, packaging themselves, and tirelessly promoting and marketing themselves amidst the flood of information; others, driven by a mindset of not flaunting their wealth, focusing on self-improvement, hiding their strengths and biding their time, or building up strength quietly, keep their heads down and work diligently without making a sound."}
{"trans": "In reality, why do \"war of words\" always spread extensively and fail to cease even after several months? What forces are adding fuel to the flames behind the scenes? And what exactly is subtly influencing netizens' judgments and thoughts? Not only ordinary netizens but even some website administrators are greatly puzzled by this."}
{"trans": "That evening, he spread out his manuscript paper, ready to write an article to earn back those twenty yuan. That night, the title of his essay was: On the Necessity and Possibility of Morality? He declared: In this decadent era of material desires, we must raise the banner of morality against the enslavement of materialism. That night, his essay surged forward with fervor—intense, indignant, heartfelt, persuasive, impassioned, gut-wrenching, sincere, sharp, unrestrained, fluid, soaring, and unstoppable..."}
{"trans": "The Discourse Essay must be visionary. As an official-style essay, the most fundamental characteristics of the Discourse Essay are its elevated perspective and lofty theme. Writing such an essay requires focusing on long-term interests, looking beyond the surface to understand the essence, adeptly adopting a broad and commanding perspective, and skillfully elevating the theme. This means that the resulting article must embody a noble intellectual horizon, eschewing any pandering to vulgar tastes, and certainly avoiding lowbrow content or the expression of grievances and complaints."}
{"trans": "He is often melancholic, but his melancholy is a compassion shown to the suffering. When he smiles, his smile is like the longing of those who seek the unknown, like stardust falling on a child's eyelids, and like a piece of bread in the throat."}
{"trans": "If you look upward, you will also see how evenly proportioned her shoulders are! They are like twin lambs, or like two peaks of jade—slender as the autumn mountains, smooth as the autumn waters. Above the shoulders lies the face, praised and celebrated by all."}
{"trans": "Even the lotus has the tragedy of being executed along with nine branches of the family. Lotus upon lotus, the thousand fingers of the lotus petals grasp one summer and release another. Now it is the ghostly rain of an autumn night, splashing on the fragmented duckweed-covered water, like a disheveled, blind-eyed Chopin tormenting the thousand-keyed piano."}
{"trans": "Listening to Zen under the moon, the essence grows more profound; discussing swords under the moon, hearts grow more sincere; conversing on poetry under the moon, charm grows more subtle; facing a beauty under the moon, affection grows deeper. Methods of enjoying the moon: when it is bright and clear, one should gaze up; when hazy, one should look down. The spring breeze is like wine; the summer breeze like tea; the autumn breeze like smoke; the winter breeze like ginger and mustard."}
{"trans": "He rode the waves of blood in a small red boat, gracefully arriving in this damp and cold world. His final leap was propelled by surging heatwaves out of the gate of life, like mud and sand swept away in a flood. The baby's excited cries shattered like clashing glass cups."}
{"trans": "If China had one more melancholic writer, this north-facing study should be held accountable. Seated in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel as though I’m refrigerated in a freezer, like a fruit heavily laden with the warmth of the south. By day, I seem to sink into the ocean's depths, where the profound silence plays a somber, grey melody."}
{"trans": "The red candle possesses a spirit. She spares no thought for her own life, yet she profoundly cherishes it. Each time she nears the end, the charred wick strains upward convulsively, holding firm high in the flame, much like a warrior struck by a sudden bullet, freezing mid-air into an unyielding sculpture before heavily collapsing into a pool of fiery blood..."}
{"trans": "Looking out at the sky upon stepping outside, the heavens, marked by their celestial pathways, inspire introspection of one's own conduct. Morning dew settles after the rain, and the sun emerges, with glistening droplets everywhere, all shining together—one sun giving rise to countless suns. There’s no need to sweep away the old cobweb in the corner; let the dust settle, and over time, the strands thicken like the twisting roots of an ancient tree, forming a three-dimensional mural that speaks of tradition, of modernity, ever fresh with each revisit."}
{"trans": "Spring always knocks first on the bamboo gate of the garden, then lights the torches that were extinguished last year, one by one. At this moment, winter, left alone in its empty domain, flees the battlefield like a desolate wolf amid the sudden flames. The flames leave its lonely gaze disoriented, and the earth's floral skirt leads it astray."}
{"trans": "The methods of punishing evil are often more evil than evil itself; killing the innocent is as effortless as cutting chives. Beneath the banners of loyalty, filial piety, integrity, and righteousness, there is nothing but the glint of blades and shadows of swords. The cost of grand, majestic ideals is a battlefield littered with corpses. The fundamental value of life becomes mere dry grass beneath the hooves of warhorses; the right to survival for ordinary people is but a few bubbles at the edge of a whirlpool."}
{"trans": "——The celestial sound, an infinite mystery, the siege of the finite by the infinite, or God's stern yet gentle command. Music is the omniscient and omnipotent God of notes, who is both the Creator—arranging and fixing the positions of the notes—and the Savior—if the notes can listen and follow the unceasing, untiring performance."}
{"trans": "All over this winding stretch of water, what meets the eye is a silken field of leaves, reaching rather high above the surface, like the skirts of dancing girls in all their grace. Here and there, layers of leaves are dotted with white lotus blossoms, some in demure bloom, others in shy bud, like scattering pearls, or twinkling stars, or beauties just out of the bath."}
{"trans": "Therefore, for a city, if all that is encountered and seen is youthful and beautiful, it must be that the time has not yet come, and the strings of the zither are not yet harmonized. This is like writing; when adjectives are like ladies in full attire and parallel sentences stand side by side like lovers, it certainly has not yet entered the true way of writing. The ultimate state of writing is like sparse wutong trees on an old street, an old seat beneath the trees, and idle chatter among those seated—refined and unhurried."}
{"trans": "The suffering of individual households does not affect the world's happiness. Summer arrives uncontrollably, and the silk tree flowers, like pink powder puffs, brush against the lonely and desolate windowsill of the hospital ward. The girl's head had become polygonal, with long-healed cranial sutures resembling cracked earth, stretching thin skin over gaping hollows as an inner demon swelled in all directions."}
{"trans": "Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a southern fruit, heavy with ripeness, chilled in a refrigerator. By day, I seem to be submerged deep in the sea, where the silent darkness plays a symphony of gray. At night, I seem to hear the sound of Eskimo sleds gliding, while the long beard of the North Star hangs down, clinking and chiming, striking strings of white stalactites."}
{"trans": "They are as serene as the bright moon, not intending to disturb anyone, yet genuinely stirring the surroundings far and wide, truly exemplifying the phrase \"the moonrise startles the mountain birds.\" Compared to Tao Yuanming's tranquility, Wang Wei's serenity carries a touch of aristocratic elegance and more refined artistry. His brilliance lies in embodying nobility more plainly than the common folk and crafting his art more naturally than nature itself."}
{"trans": "Even the brown tea table is painted with emotion, a gentle little rectangle bearing all the lively scene above. There is another, larger one, also adorned with magnolia blossoms, thin and bright, resembling both jade and crystal, like the cool sensation of the jade fish Empress Yang held in her mouth when her tooth ached. The resilient lines of the winter jasmine stretch and contract with effort; its control over life is both calm and domineering."}
{"trans": "Vast and hazy, I return to the great wilderness!\" Reading this passage, what I felt was not sorrow but beauty—a sensation akin to reading in the Records of the Grand Historian about Jing Ke, dressed in white, crossing the Yi River to assassinate the King of Qin, full of vivid imagery. Imagine a young master from a wealthy family, having seen through the ways of the world, standing barefoot and bald-headed in the snow, draped in a red cloak, bidding farewell to his father—what a magnificent scene it was!"}
{"trans": "We cannot bypass that dark, humiliating, and indifferent era of Chengde, just as approaching the Mogao Caves inevitably means confronting that ugly and desolate Taoist pagoda. No matter how brilliantly colorful and magnificent Dunhuang may be in memory, it ultimately cannot fill the vast emptiness of the Library Cave, cannot wash away the stark pallor within the Thousand Buddha Caves, and cannot soothe the bleeding wounds of an ancient nation on the distant horizon."}
{"trans": "Forgetting visits us with increasing frequency and becomes a lifelong friend. I then use this friend to sift through memories, for what is forgotten is not worth remembering. The subconscious manipulates memory, much like the wind directing a kite on an invisible level. A new, formidable weave forms an uneven sieve of memory, leaving behind coagulated lumps like cheese, sweet yet concealing hard, gritty bits that grate against the teeth."}
{"trans": "His chest was grand and upright, harboring the earth-shattering roars of ancestors chasing fierce beasts. His pelvis was sharply recessed, with sharply protruding bones indicating where powerful muscle groups had once attached, pulling the entire torso in gecko-like climbs like the ropes of Yellow River trackers. And his limbs, like the long and beautiful tusks of an African elephant, emitted a smooth, creamy glow."}
{"trans": "It wasn't until years later that I let go of my lingering resentment and came to admit: that day was a treacherous bend in the journey of my life. What drove me to destroy that withered rose painting wasn't the art teacher's mockery, but the sight of your dazzling talent—so brilliant that I broke my own paintbrush in a gesture of regret. What is regret like? It's like a small mole on your body—only you know its exact location and how it came to be."}
{"trans": "I was combing my hair on the balcony, shedding it like falling leaves, strands drifting down in waves, brushing against my arms like night rain. Far and near, many car horns sounded in frantic cries; the sky gradually darkened, spreading out on all sides like a vast lake of mist and glow. From a ground-floor window across the way, a wisp of pale cooking smoke rose hesitantly, as if unsure where the sky might be."}
{"trans": "She carried a water jar in each hand, reminding me of a woman walking with a spirited air on a tightrope. And all this due to her waist—her waist was truly too supple; as Bai Shui put it, it was so soft that it felt like I was eating Suzhou's chewy malt sugar candy. But it wasn't just her waist; as my diary aptly noted: She possessed a set of curves that could rival the clouds and compete with the water's moon, weaving a vast and bewildering net!"}
{"trans": "“Because of your language, you remain silent, sinking to the deepest depths, allowing yourself to disappear.” Losing language, thus losing oneself, losing the essence of existence — Yang Lian thus recognizes that he has become a “ghost.” A ghost drifts between cities, observing coldly (like an insect, a ghost is also an “it,” capable only of observation), observing the complete annihilation of “meaning.” There is the sea, yet the harbor holds no significance for you."}
{"trans": "The streetlights stand far apart from one another; between the stretches of light lie stretches of darkness. My shadow emerges in the light, then vanishes into the darkness. A wind from nowhere rustles the colorful fallen leaves in waves, as if stirring the impressions of life. I feel like this empty, unfathomable wind, only able to grasp my own existence when shedding and swirling up the vibrant leaves."}
{"trans": "But we, standing on the open land—my father, my brother, relatives, and many fellow villagers who had shed sweat, endured scorching sun, and weathered storms—stood still, listening to the distant thunder, with no one making a move to seek shelter from the northwestern rain. Our hearts were heavier than the parched sky; everyone remained silent, for our hearts were also like skies about to rain, and this inner rain seemed even more poignant and relentless than the northwestern downpour."}
{"trans": "Imagine if Tang Bohu and Emperor Qianlong were considered \"first-rate poets of ancient China\"—then we might as well quietly set the entire *Complete Tang Poems* ablaze. The same applies to calligraphy: an astonishingly high price paid for a work of mediocre quality is like a heap of gold crushing the scales of Chinese calligraphic history. Faced with this situation, I once sighed deeply: \"When the pulse of culture fades, small hills are hailed as peaks; when strong wings have flown far, tattered feathers pose as rocs.\""}
{"trans": "The onset was abrupt, as if the girl had received a sudden decree from the heavens, spasming without any warning. The limp girl curled up like an extremely rigid rolling pin, every muscle gleaming like iron. Her small body arched like a bowstring drawn to shoot an eagle, rebounding on the snow-white hospital bed. Countless beads of sweat dripped and splattered from this grotesque human arch, much like the melting snow from eaves when spring blossoms arrive."}
{"trans": "This unleashed force, solitary yet powerful, adheres to norms while breaking them, brimming with both intoxication and poetic charm, closely resembling the Dionysian spirit described by Nietzsche. Driven by this Dionysian spirit, Zhang Xu wielded his brush like staggering drunken steps—swaying, dancing, and moving with effortless grace and充沛 energy, completing every motion in one fluid sequence before tossing his cup aside with a laugh and drifting into deep slumber. Unbeknownst to Zhang Xu, his drunken dance was also the very stride of Tang Dynasty culture."}
{"trans": "But just as I was holding my breath and listening intently, they suddenly, all at once, fell silent again. These cicadas startled me once more! Like a rope, the cicadas' song had tightly bound my heart, only to suddenly release it without any warning, leaving my heart unpreparedly scattered apart—like a wave leaping vigorously toward the sky, only to accidentally crash upon the beach! When did summer step over the threshold and come in? I hadn't even noticed!"}
{"trans": "I have shed tears for your humiliation and despair. My tears flowed like a stream, clear as crystal, yet they could not wash away your thick grime, only removing the veil from my eyes; these tears could not moisten your stony hearts in the slightest, only quenching the flame of anxious eagerness in my heart. Now, for your suffering, I laugh, and this laughter roars like thunder, not coming after the storm, but resounding before it."}
{"trans": "I gradually came to understand that in the face of disaster, one should not use the grammar of disaster; there is another kind of grammar that leads directly to the poetic realm of spiritual freedom. From then on, my state of life was never the same. Every time I read Zhuangzi's chapters such as \"Autumn Floods,\" \"Free and Easy Wandering,\" \"Discussion on Making All Things Equal,\" and \"Under Heaven,\" it felt like looking at electrocardiograms related to myself. For such an intimately close ancient sage, it is difficult for me to provide a calm and fair commentary, so I can only keep a certain distance."}
{"trans": "You press your forehead against the gold-woven embroidery. When the sun was on this side, it heated the golden threads until they were scalding hot, but now they have cooled. People of the past toiled through their entire lives, and what they did gradually became covered in dust; when their descendants hung out the laundry, they shook the dust off again, making it dance in the yellow sunlight. If memories had a scent, it would be that of camphor, sweet and reassuring, like a clearly remembered joy, sweet and wistful, like a forgotten sorrow."}
{"trans": "It is this very extent that brings them closer to life and allows us, even after millennia, to feel connected to them. I imagine Yang Guifei’s liveliness as a kind of ceramic warming pot—smooth as jade, placed at the foot of the bed. When the water inside gradually cools, it evokes a gentle, lingering melancholy. Su Qing, on the other hand, is like a small red-clay stove with its own independent fire, visible in its blazing flames and audible in its crackling bursts. Yet it is harder to tend to, requiring constant additions of coal and firewood, with smoke that chokes."}
{"trans": "Again, like booming waves or raging seas, slapping against the sediment of emotions in your heart. In an instant, you feel the cicadas' chorus sweeps away the gentle melancholy you’ve been clutching tightly, like wild waves washing over the sand. The rapid urgency of the cicadas' song suddenly stops at its highest, most intense note, much like a splendid piece of writing torn apart abruptly, scattering resonant phrases like gold and stone, which then fall silent and become fragmented passages, leaving only a sense of wistfulness and sorrow. Is it not, after all, the song of life itself?"}
{"trans": "Here thrives vibrant youth, here beats passion aflame in crimson hearts; there are no listless old souls in miniature, only robust elders with a youthful spirit. The silvery moon meanders languidly across the vast, empty sky, as if shedding tears of sorrow, lamenting her own solitude. ... And then there's the swimming pool, ever resembling a benevolent grandmother, her face creased with wrinkles as she smiles. When she sees lively children leaping into the water like little mermaids with a splash, she bursts into immense, joyous silver sprays."}
{"trans": "For millennia, it had been a lost wilderness. On the far side of the wilderness were the faint, shadowy figures of unknown great artisans; on this side stood a panicked modern woman. The kilns on both sides blazed fiercely, like two beacon towers separated by countless mountains and rivers, yet the signals they transmitted were precise and unmistakable. Many other beacon towers were linked to war, but these two were not. Across the bloodshed of the Three Kingdoms, the struggles of the Sui and Tang, and the battles of the Song, Yuan, Ming, and Qing dynasties, only these two purest wisps of smoke echoed each other from afar."}
{"trans": "The fragmentation of Lin Daiyu lies in her profound and unforgettable love; the fragmentation of San Mao stems from her sudden clarity and transcendence after enduring countless hardships; the fragmentation of Van Gogh is the sun's golden knives causing him incessant agony in the light; the fragmentation of Beethoven is the collision of the spiritual black and white keys striking the tragic and heroic movement of life. If the fragmentation of ordinary individuals reveals the purest and most beautiful sparks of humanity, then the fragmentation of these exceptional souls is like silver fireworks blooming across the sky above our heads."}
{"trans": "The face is washed several times a day, yet it never seems clean; the eyes are never washed in a lifetime, yet they remain forever bright. Unused spaces don’t warrant the function of a mop or broom, so there’s no need to spend that money—after all, people are active, natural dust-repelling pearls. Strangely, the air doesn’t thin out despite the cramped space. To make human breath visible, cigarettes serve as tangible air: inhale one puff, exhale three, and the smoke curls upward to the ceiling. Under this auspicious cloud, one can first observe the richness of earthly things before lifting their gaze to contemplate the vastness of the universe."}
{"trans": "To know oneself without knowing others is merely to confine oneself to a corner, a method of growing old and dying without mutual interaction; it is nothing more than being a summer insect that cannot speak of ice, a frog at the bottom of a well, or a donkey in a mill. Only by understanding others can one truly possess self-awareness; just like Princess Iron Fan's magical fan, one must be able to release it before one can retract it. The more one knows, the broader one's connections become; by dispersing oneself throughout the world and immersing into all things, observing their size and shape, their weight and density, one can then dissect with the finest precision and gradually, bit by bit, recognize one's true self."}
{"trans": "The song, like drifting clouds and flowing water, washes away worries and immerses the listener. It also resembles surging waves and roaring tides, striking the emotions buried deep within one's heart. In an instant, the cicada's chirp feels like a raging tide washing away the light sorrow tightly clutched in hand. The urgency of the cicada's song suddenly halts at its highest note, much like a splendid piece of writing torn apart abruptly, scattering resonant words and phrases across the ground like the clinking of metal and stone. Then, it fades into fragmented verses, leaving behind only a sense of melancholy and wistfulness."}
{"trans": "What is there about nothingness? The matters of the divine are unknown to humans; human affairs lie in constructing and perpetuating meaning amidst the siege of fate—perhaps helplessly—thus saving both the present and eternity. Therefore, \"eternal recurrence\" is by no means a \"comprehensive affirmation of earthly life,\" but merely states that humans cannot escape earthly life, not even in death. As for affirmation, it refers to the pursuit and transcendence toward eternity, that is, the earth's gaze toward the sky—that vast music has always filled both heaven and earth."}
{"trans": "Viewing Venerable Xiao Yun's Chan paintings offers a completely different experience. It feels like reading Tao Yuanming and Wang Wei's pastoral poems late at night—just a few simple strokes and light inkwork that don't stir up turbulent emotions but instead calm our restlessness. It's not about adding something to our hearts but rather cleansing away the worldly worries that already fill them. Like a mountain stream after a heavy rain, initially murky but becoming entirely clear once the skies clear, with all the mud and filth washed away."}
{"trans": "The sound, now slow, now rapid, now high, now low, now loud, now soft, now intermittent, now continuous, sometimes resembles the resonance of gold and jade, sometimes the toll of a grand bell, sometimes the cascade of pearls large and small falling upon a jade plate, sometimes the sinking of red and white corals into the sea, sometimes the strumming of a plain zither, sometimes the dance of thunderbolts, sometimes the chorus of a hundred birds, sometimes the swift descent of a falcon upon a hare. My imagination soars, unrestrained; my heart blossoms with joy, and my pen glides effortlessly. Lifeless words seem to come alive, and I feel once again brimming with youthful vitality. Rarely in my life have I experienced such a spiritual state, one that is even harder to convey to others."}
{"trans": "Perhaps, clouds are meant to traverse the heavens, unlike the sun with its fiery-wheeled feet, so they do not descend to earth to receive my warm hospitality; it is merely my illusion, though an illusion far too beautiful. If the blue sky is a wordless celestial book, then clouds must be its unannotated footnotes, and my swift tire tracks translating the language of clouds onto the road surface are the latest published commentary. The sky narrates in shifting shades of blue, the clouds depict with pristine strokes, and then entrust my eyes to print—we are all telling the story of Kuafu."}
{"trans": "I couldn't conveniently take it out to eat on the plane. Upon returning to the US, I tried it and found it overly greasy and too spicy—nothing like the sausage rolls I occasionally had from my father's. Next door to our home in Shanghai was the newly relocated wartime Tianjin Kiessling Café. Every dawn, they baked bread, sending out an olfactory alarm—a magnificent, fragrant aroma that surged through the air with the force of a sweeping wind, yet it was the gentlest of alarm clocks. Unfortunately, it always went off at the wrong time, needlessly waking people up, much like the vexing beauty of spring that leaves one helpless. Having such a \"fragrant\" neighbor was truly a nuisance."}
{"trans": "Happiness in life is like the sugar cube used to entice a child to take medicine, or like the electric rabbit that lures dogs to race in a greyhound track. A few minutes or a few days of happiness earn us a lifetime of enduring much suffering. We hope it comes, we hope it stays, and we hope it comes again—these three phrases encapsulate the entire history of human endeavor. While we pursue and wait, life stealthily slips away. Perhaps we are merely chips consumed by time, living a life only to serve as sacrificial offerings to the years of that existence, never truly contemplating happiness."}
{"trans": "There is a dark olive-green silk that sweeps across large, shadowy figures, brimming with wind and thunder. There is also a Japanese silk fabric, pale lake-colored, shimmering with wood and water patterns; at intervals, two plum blossoms the size of tea cups float upon the water, etched sharply as if drawn with iron and silver, resembling the stained-glass windows of medieval chapels, with red glass edged heavily in iron. The most common colors on the market are those that cannot be named—neither blue, nor gray, nor yellow—only suitable for backgrounds. These are neutral colors, also known as protective colors, civilized colors, or blended colors."}
{"trans": "it's derived from her movements; with every step she takes, every graceful stretch she makes, every sidelong glance she casts, every slight nod she gives, even the gentle sway of her sleeves or the soft flutter of her skirt, it all flows like honey rippling in a breeze—how can we not delight and marvel? What is most adorable about her is that supple waist of hers; in olden times people praised willow branches swaying in the wind, and Dream of the Red Chamber described Qingwen’s waist as slender like a water snake’s—all emphasizing the delicate softness of her waist. But the waistline that delights me is simply like Suzhou's peanut brittle, filling my whole mouth with sweetness and making my teeth feel tender just imagining it. With a waist so soft, her hands and feet naturally possess an air of extraordinary grace."}
{"trans": "Beside me, several bottles lay askew, their contents nearly drained. It's a pity I don't drink, for in such moments, taking a few sips would surely be a sublime pleasure. \"Raising my cup, I invite the bright moon,\" and the moon shyly slips into my glass. A gentle breeze passes by, rustling the trees on the hillsides, their branches swaying, making the flickering lights appear even more elusive, like mischievous children playing hide-and-seek. Paired with the shimmering scales of light dancing on the river surface, it’s as if they are performing a harmonious, enchanting melody. What kind of earthly dream is this?"}
{"trans": "I can no longer clearly articulate how, with a real sun shining on the stage, such a profound sense of melancholy could arise. There is a space where art and reality overlap, blurring into a hazy ambiguity—like holding a match and lighting it in broad daylight, where the faint orange flame flickers almost imperceptibly, yet one becomes acutely aware of one’s own hand, itself a transient object in the sunlight... The maid on stage sang for a while, then, holding a tea tray, moved with the grace of parting blossoms and brushing aside willow branches, passing through countless rooms and doorways until she reached the study. There, she bowed deeply to the young master, raising the tea tray level with her eyebrows."}
{"trans": "I saw a calico cat lounging obliquely beneath a section of dilapidated, abandoned broken wall, while morning glories bloomed in a riot of deep blues and brilliant purples. The cat stretched lazily, indifferent to it all. In the hazy night, I saw a streetlamp casting the shadow of a utility box on the sidewalk chaotically onto a white construction site wall, where it intermingled with the dappled, swaying branches of roadside trees, creating a play of light and shadow that resembled the balcony from which Romeo serenaded Juliet. I saw the face of the poet Zhou Mengdie, just as I waved to see him off, perfectly framed in the small window of a moving bus, as if the entire vehicle were solemnly serving as his picture frame."}
{"trans": "You see that innocent heart, so pure yet full of love for all, in the faint mist of dawn, however much you beckon, never returns to its abode; how \"lacking\" is that! Thus, Mr. Pingbo felt stifled, and so honestly, like the gentle wind whispering among the green trees of spring, softly and intently, recounted his memorable yet elusive \"childhood\" to you. Though he cannot linger in that \"childhood\" forever, if he can call upon a few companions to wander there awhile, it might alleviate his sense of emptiness, and the taste of melancholy would no longer cling persistently to the tip of his tongue."}
{"trans": "You could also say it is the starting point for the Chinese people's journey toward modernity, but which nation's steps toward modernity have been as hurried, flustered, self-doubting, and chaotic as those in Shanghai? You could also say it is an urban civilization that rose in opposition to agricultural culture, but what other urban civilization has, like Shanghai, always been subject to the coveting, fragmentation, encirclement, and overshadowing of an immensely vast rural force? In short, it is a great paradox: when you fix your gaze on its filth, it suddenly radiates dazzling brilliance, and when you worship its might, it turns around to show you its scar-riddled back wall."}
{"trans": "However, the reality was quite the opposite. Sitting quietly there, I listened to the raindrops falling overhead, and in that moment, sound surpassed silence, filling my heart with boundless joy—as if I had sipped celestial nectar or inhaled sublime wisdom, feeling almost ethereal and transcendent. The sound varied in pace, pitch, volume, and rhythm—now slow, now urgent; now high, now low; now resonant, now subdued; now continuous, now intermittent. At times, it resembled the chime of gold and jade; at others, the solemn tones of ancient bells; sometimes like large and small pearls dropping onto a jade plate, and other times like red and white corals sinking into the sea. It could be as gentle as plucking a plain zither, or as fierce as dancing thunderbolts; now like a chorus of a hundred birds, now like a hare startled by a falcon's swoop. My thoughts drifted endlessly, unrestrained, my heart blossomed with delight, and inspiration flowed effortlessly from my pen."}
{"trans": "Amidst the vibrant billboards and shops, car horns blared incessantly; he was like the man from the ancient legend who dreamed of the golden millet, yet he had merely slept and awakened without experiencing such a dream—leaving him with an even deeper sense of desolation. ... The Taoist priest approached the entrance of a hardware store, prostrated himself in worship, though of course no one gave him money, and he seemed to pay no heed to anyone, merely bowing vaguely before rising. Once on his feet again, he began tapping—\"clack, clack\"—transitioning to the front of the neighboring tobacco and paper shop, where he once more \"knelt down upon the dusty ground,\" his head tilted askew, his movements like a dark, sluggish flow, slowly unfurling like a black chrysanthemum."}
{"trans": "So what? Birds sing in spring, crickets chirp in autumn, mosquitoes buzz like thunder in summer, and at night insects stir while birds sleep. Wind and rain do not come every day; without visitors, dogs do not bark, and hens that lay no eggs do not cluck. Only humans use language, actions, and machines to create sounds anytime, anywhere. Even when alone in a room with no one to respond, one can play a gramophone, listen to the radio, or even produce thunder-like snoring while asleep. Language, of course, is not merely sound, but when it is unpleasant, unwanted, or heard indistinctly through walls or over distances, words lose their edges and contours, turning into a swelling and shrinking clamor, as meaningless as the crowing of roosters or the barking of dogs."}
{"trans": "As time passes, the past remains forever gone, unable to be rewound to the moment of first encounter when faces and blossoms met; yet in human memory, the lingering charm or residual wounds of bygone days often surge like waves against the shore, extending the present into a continuation of past elegance or sorrow, growing ever more distant yet persistently alive. If life is a pre-bound book with blank pages already numbered, the disturbances from past affections are like pressing the pen too hard while writing a certain page, causing the ink to seep through to the following pages, leaving an indelible mark. There is no need to tear out the old pages in pursuit of relief, just as there is no reason to destroy the Yellow Crane Tower once the crane has flown away; however, it is essential to spread open the old history under the lamplight, to proceed where one should proceed and to stop where one should stop."}
{"trans": "The Great Northwest is a land of barren basalt mountains and vast deserts where lone plumes of smoke rise straight into the sky. As a geologist, you carry a large canvas field bag over your shoulder, having journeyed tirelessly for twenty years. Two decades of tents, like tiny boats adrift in seas of sand, under the cold, curved moon—could the bells of Hanshan Temple beyond Suzhou truly \"reach the guest boat at midnight\"? Your wife, that exquisite beauty, gazes after you, her face woven with a net of longing, fishing for a distant loving heart. You return once a year, each time planting a cluster of tender bamboo by the gate. But then you leave again, leaving her with nothing but the bamboo leaves' pattern of \"个\" characters."}
{"trans": "If life is a pre-bound book with numbered blank pages, then the disturbances caused by past affections are like pressing too hard while writing on a certain page, allowing the ink to seep through to the subsequent pages, leaving an indelible mark. There is certainly no need to destroy the old pages in pursuit of relief, just as there is no reason to demolish the Yellow Crane Tower once the crane has flown away. Yet, it is necessary to unfold the old history under the lamplight, to proceed where one should proceed and to stop where one should stop. After embracing life in its entirety, one can view both past events and new matters with generosity, granting them their rightful place and significance. If it is a beautiful memory, one can discern what new branches sprout from its buds; if it is a sorrowful event, one can also see a tender shoot reaching from cloudy days into the sunshine."}
{"trans": "Everything feels distant and unfamiliar to me, even my own shadow under the moonlight appears more hazy than mist. Just as I was about to turn and go to sleep, somehow I hesitated for a moment, causing the fleeting remnants of my dream to abruptly pause—though it soon sped away again like an arrow released from its bowstring."}
{"trans": "What is ultimately hoped for is merely an aesthetic support. It is like looking up at the scene of dark clouds swiftly rolling by when a ship sinking in an icy sea is utterly beyond rescue; it is like glancing down at the pattern of blood splattering when there is absolutely no escape from a flurry of blades. Aesthetic support is the final support."}
{"trans": "What we gather from the past and future is but seed after seed,  \nWhen you are a wish wandering in the mist, so too am I.  \nWe seek each other, and from our longing grows a dream,  \nUnceasing is that dream, boundless is that dream."}
{"trans": "In such purity, the dish is oneself, the cook is oneself, and the person eating is oneself. Just as love is oneself, the one who knows this love is oneself, and the one who remembers this love is still oneself. One savors oneself bite by bite, holding up the cup of time, intoxicating oneself in the process."}
{"trans": "The long pants clung tightly, making it hard to lift a foot. My heart was as simple as a sheet of paper, as blank as a newborn baby, bidding farewell to the sea, to a lonely seagull circling in the sky. I will return, to speak of the dust of the farthest corners of the world. Picking up the umbrella and shoes, picking up all the myriad things of human life."}
{"trans": "Unpredictable. I only hope that even as a human flaw, it should present itself in a dignified manner. Like the frowning sighs of a noble warrior, not the chaotic brawls of ragged soldiers in the dead of night; like the millennia-long standoff between two snow-capped peaks, not the tangled mess of vines strangling a tree trunk."}
{"trans": "That night, the plateau was extremely beautiful. The sky resembled a deep blue ritual vessel, seemingly fired during the Jingtai era of the Ming Dynasty, profound and boundless. Through the massive moon, like a silver table, one could still glimpse the metallic blue light behind it. The moonlight, unable to rival the dye of the blue sky, drifted like diluted ink, wisp by wisp, ethereally."}
{"trans": "Watching the same movie repeatedly is like chewing food that has been spit out. At that moment, our heads turned golden, as if covered with wheat awns. I recall a character in Gorky’s book saying that lovers from youth should not meet again later in life, like a skeleton rising from the ground…"}
{"trans": "With eyes closed, I think of it; with eyes open, I crave it. And when all this rushes at me, nearly overwhelming, I hardly know what I truly want anymore, only feeling a heart aching persistently, as if tightly bound by silken threads, scorched by drops of candle wax, tossed upon the vast, desolate sea."}
{"trans": "The faintest echo of your sobbing shall become its life veiled; like your greatest soul, it is concealed and hidden. When life speaks, all winds turn into words; when life speaks again, the smile upon your lips and the tears in your eyes shall also turn into words."}
{"trans": "Consequently, the collective cultural identity has increasingly faded. As seasons come and go, with plum blossoms withering and cranes aging, culture has turned into an aimless extravagance, and closed-off moral perfection has led to overall immorality. The rapid advancement of civilization has thus been negated, leaving behind only scattered plum petals and crane feathers, like bookmarks tucked into the annals of the national spirit."}
{"trans": "Using science and philosophy as standards to grant a pass to religious spirit is like using intellect and reasoning to engage in love—it inevitably suppresses the passion of life and exhausts the charm of love. Replacing religious spirit with political and economic policies is akin to treating social status and wealth as prerequisites for marriage, willingly reducing children to breeding machines and becoming spiritual eunuchs."}
{"trans": "Indeed, all forms of devastation are specific, and all grievances are difficult to articulate, which makes those answers questionable. What remains unquestionable is the outcome—withered grass and rubble, bearing witness to disasters from ancient times to the present. I am willing to confront all this in perilous situations without any protective mechanisms, just like removing gloves to touch the scars of the elderly."}
{"trans": "Now, I have written these many pages. I see myself as a child, copying a passage from a long hymn that angels sang when God shaped the first man. Or perhaps I am like an illiterate person, memorizing a sentence from a book written by wisdom, inscribed on the pages of emotion before time began."}
{"trans": "Even the grandest events spanning millennia or the most monumental feats connecting vast distances, if they belong to culture, are often borne by aged shoulders. Like a smuggler, like a fugitive, dodging and inquiring discreetly along the way, searching for a place of entrustment. The decision to entrust is always written in a will, destined never to articulate the cultural meaning of one's life while still alive."}
{"trans": "There is no doubt about the outcome: withered grass and rubble bear witness to disasters from ancient times to the present. I willingly confront all this in peril without any protective mechanism, just like taking off gloves to touch the scars of an elderly person. Such touching often provokes deep reflection: as the foundation of our lives, Chinese civilization is also scarred, yet how has it avoided a complete collapse?"}
{"trans": "Could anyone possibly deliver a ready-made meaning along with your birth certificate? The very fact of birth is a demand for meaning from the one born—it requires you to seek or create meaning, much like a publishing contract that pays an advance with a deadline lasting a lifetime. Of course, you are not the creditor but the debtor; it is life that demands meaning from you, leaving you no room to complain about anyone."}
{"trans": "The uneven ink, the headlines in red, the names crossed out, the rows of exclamation marks, the restrained appeals, and the repeated corrections all combined into a terrifying sound that rushed toward me. It was as if just a few strands of white hair on a spiderweb in the corner of a room, or a half-torn piece of cloth among withered leaves on a treetop, could instantly transport us back to that era we dare not recall."}
{"trans": "Some land on the vegetable-picking woman's bun, some cling to the swallow's black coat, some slide into the small river to play in the water. The river, like a thousand flute-playing wanderers, accompanies the singing joy of children after school. When mischievous children place their books atop their yellow leather caps and wade across the river holding their two shoes, might the spore babies pop out from the flute holes, bite onto the children's clothes, and finally return to the soil of the wild fern mother?"}
{"trans": "Soul, come back! Return to your old dwelling place. When he spoke Hokkien and made everyone roar with laughter, when he spoke Mandarin and left people bewildered, why did he never defend himself? Here, his Chu dialect is as profound as the heavens, earth, and mountains, as grand as the sky and the spirits. Every word from the master of ceremonies, like my father reciting the \"Memorial of Parting and Lament,\" is sorrowful and poignant, each syllable striking you deeply."}
{"trans": "He was too thin, his withered skin unable to fill the gaps between his ribs, making the round cake seem like a steel bridge spanning over his ribcage. The violent, heavy heartbeat was like a bleeding sun, burning hollowly, emitting sounds of flames and caverns. Mei Ying had heard Yue Beizhi's heartbeat—deep and resonant, pulsing steadily and rhythmically through his well-developed muscles, like coal buried deep within the earth's crust."}
{"trans": "From one inn to another, never settling in a mountain village or by the water's edge, what talisman is sufficient for me to pray for? Perhaps it is youth, but how fleeting it is. I am like one who has unearthed treasure, carrying pearls, gold, and silver in a leaky net bag, only to find it growing lighter along the way—youth has already scattered into dust. Perhaps it is the scriptures and classics, but how can a mind full of knowledge mend the broken mirror in my hands?"}
{"trans": "On the hills of my hometown, when greeting someone from afar, it was never the soft \"Hey—\" of city folk, nor the deliberately astonished \"Wow—\" of southerners. The \"Hey\" and \"Wow\" wouldn't travel far before being swallowed by the mountains. Only the deep, resonant, prolonged, and desolate \"Eh ha—\" could soar like an eagle, lingering in the air. Now, that eagle's feather descends like mist from the sky, and an endless wave of homesickness, hot and sharp, fills Shen Zhanping's chest."}
{"trans": "Quickly escape the political quagmire that you yourself don't even fully understand, and chase after the long-lost poetic sentiment. Chasing poetic sentiment is chasing the self—the self once familiar to all, clung to by a wife, the self that was thought to be found but instead lost. This time, turning back to chase it, there are morning clouds to see you off, rivers to bear witness, the cries of apes to encourage you, and countless mountains to make way. Thus, the boat of life, burdened with ever-increasing weight, once again becomes a light vessel."}
{"trans": "Although an airplane can be imagined as Zhuangzi's carefree wanderings or Liezi's wind-riding journey, it is not enduringly captivating. How unlike the long-distance train journey, with its hypnotic rhythm and ever-changing scenery—looking out from the window, one feels both in the human world and as if gliding beyond it. Thus, when traveling abroad, wherever the clanging twin tracks can reach, I always stand on the platform—truly a \"long pavilion\"—waiting for the train, with its masculine beauty, to thunderously and unstoppably charge into the station, ready to carry me to distant lands."}
{"trans": "Confronting prominence is the norm; confronting officialdom are the common people. More concealed than the lush grass and dense trees in the mountains and forests is the ordinary life of common folk disappearing into a small town. The concealment in the mountains and forests still retains and flaunts a kind of aloofness, and such aloof concealment is ultimately insincere. The concealment in the streets of a small town not only avoids deliberately tormenting and destroying life but also allows one to live very comfortably, nestling life into a quiet and convenient corner, almost melting away from the outside in. Thus, it becomes the highest form of concealment. Perhaps calling it concealment is too narrow; in my mind, scenes like a small bridge, flowing water, and homes, or the longing for water shield and perch, are all ecological images of a religious philosophy of life."}
{"trans": "The vernal breeze I do not know;\nWhy should it intrude my bed curtain?"}
{"trans": "From now on I'll no longer love the fine night;  Let the moon descend the western tower!"}
{"trans": "The candle has a wick and still grieves at our parting, Shedding tears until the break of day."}
{"trans": "Chang'e must regret stealing the elixir of life,\n\nIn those vast sea-blue skies, she broods night after night."}
{"trans": "Thrice I saw the prince displayed plans for statecraft; Twice he served the court to show a loyal man's heart."}
{"trans": "\"The tripartite balance of power was shrewdly planned, And long as the highest feather in the clouds he stands.\""}
{"trans": "A song of flowers in the backyard beyond,  \nSo sad and drear that it can't be heard."}
{"trans": "Swallows that skimmed by painted eaves in bygone days are dipping now among the humble homes' doorways."}
{"trans": "Melancholy, I cannot see Fan Li again,\nIn mist-veiled trees of Five Lakes to the east men differ in view."}
{"trans": "If the east wind did not give a hand to General Zhou,  \nThe two Qiaos would have been locked in the Bronze Bird Tower in spring."}
{"trans": "Victory and failure are common things in a soldier's life; enduring humiliation makes a true man."}
{"trans": "For the Son of Heaven who reigned four decades, say,\nWas he not poorer than the Lu's of the day?"}
{"trans": "The jade tally bids the Phoenix Tower farewell,\nSteel chargers surround the Dragon City."}
{"trans": "Why should the Qiang flute complain no willows grow?\nBeyond the Gate of Jade no vernal wind will blow."}
{"trans": "Hundreds of battles fought in the desert wear through armor of gold; we'll never turn back till we capture Loulan."}
{"trans": "The moon over the mountain pass is still the moon of Chin,\n\nOn and on the expedition has found no men."}
{"trans": "At ease, the guardsmen watch the border scene,\n\nHomesick, their faces show a bitter mien."}
{"trans": "Shoot the horse to bring down the rider, capture the chief to defeat the gang."}
{"trans": "The vast sea is frozen a hundred feet deep, And gloomy clouds hang sad and dreary for ten thousand miles."}
{"trans": "Dark is the forest and grass startled by wind; Our general draws his bow at night."}
{"trans": "The desert sands look white as snow; the Goulan Mountain moon looks like a hook."}
{"trans": "At noon they weed with hoes; Their sweat drips on the soil."}
{"trans": "a steed raising red dust won a fair smile."}
{"trans": "The dappled horse and furs worth a fortune, \n\nCall the boy to exchange them for good wine, \n\nAnd together we'll melt the eternal sorrow."}
{"trans": "I mount a carriage, ready to cross the river, only to find it ice-barred;"}
{"trans": "The emperor calls; I won't board the boat,Claiming to be the Immortal of Wine afloat."}
{"trans": "Nature's artistry blends divine beauty,\nYin and Yang divide darkness from light."}
{"trans": "I have my sorrows which not even holy spirits can disperse, but you sing me a morning song, and all the world grows bright."}
{"trans": "Beholding the immensity of heaven and earth, I shed sad tears alone."}
{"trans": "Endless are trees shedding leaves shiver by shiver; \nUnlimited the Yangtze River rolls on ever."}
{"trans": "With happy ease my steed trots on and on; I've seen within one day all flowers of the capital."}
{"trans": "Master Zhuang dreams of a butterfly, yearning for the butterfly fair;  \nEmperor Wang's amorous heart in spring is given to the cuckoo's care."}
{"trans": "With towering smoke hangs the desert vast;  \nThe sun sinks round beyond the long river."}
{"trans": "Sitting alone in the quiet bamboo grove, I play my zither and whistle long."}
{"trans": "The waterfall plunges three thousand feet straight down, as if the Milky Way were falling from the ninth heaven."}
{"trans": "The window frames the western hills' eternal snow;\n\nThe door oft says to eastward-going boats hello."}
{"trans": "Wild flowers blur the traveler's captivating eyes;\nShort grass just covers the hooves of horses from the skies."}
{"trans": "The four hundred and eighty temples of the Southern Dynasties,  \nHow many towers and terraces are veiled in the misty rain?"}
{"trans": "During the Qingming Festival, rain falls thick and fast; pedestrians along the road look gloomy and wretched."}
{"trans": "But do you know by whom these young leaves are cut out? The early spring wind is as sharp as scissor blade."}
{"trans": "In April all flowers are in bloom, but the peach blossoms at the mountain temple have just begun to bloom."}
{"trans": "A bosom friend afar brings a distant land near."}
{"trans": "If my friends in the North should ask if I'm all right,\nMy heart is free of stain as ice in crystal vase."}
{"trans": "Last cup before leaving Yang Pass for the western land!"}
{"trans": "Worrying heart of mine to the moon I trust, To accompany you up to the west of Mt. Yelang.\n\n\nNotes: \n- The translation aims to maintain poetic rhythm while conveying literal meaning. \n- \"夜郎西\" is rendered geographically as \"west of Mt. Yelang\" rather than transliterated, for clarity. \n- The inversion in the first line preserves the original's lyrical quality."}
{"trans": "The Peach Blossom Pool is a thousand feet deep, yet not so deep as Wang Lun's love for me."}
{"trans": "Within the green sky the single sail vanishes. \n\nOnly the endless Yangtze River flows to the horizon."}
{"trans": "Deep green the temple 'mid bamboos, Late bell - notes o'er the glimmering flood."}
{"trans": "Approaching home, timid I grow,\n\nI dare not ask what I would know."}
{"trans": "Hearing the flute play \"Breaking Willow Branches\" tonight,\nWho wouldn't be stirred by thoughts of old friends and home?"}
{"trans": "Beacon fires burn for three months on end,\n\nA letter from home is worth ten thousand coins in gold."}
{"trans": "Who says the heart of an inch-long plant, Can require the radiance of full spring?"}
{"trans": "The flute is faintly heard mid reed flowers white; \nA line of startled snowy birds takes flight."}
{"trans": "At the head of the billows beating, There I stand, Wetting not my crimson banner steeped in dye."}
{"trans": "Countless they part, on north, south, east and west way."}
{"trans": "Beyond green willows morning chill is light; On pink apricot branches spring is running high."}
{"trans": "Early lodging on a half-traveled fragrant grass road, Still cold, awaiting rain in the late spring eve."}
{"trans": "Late at night a soft breeze brings wafts of fragrance, I did not know at dawn it would be in full bloom over the southern bough."}
{"trans": "Why need they light crimson or deep red?  \nThey are the finest 'mong flowers."}
{"trans": "If trees could feel sadness, they wouldn't appear so verdant and young!"}
{"trans": "Beside frozen dew plane leaves yellow hue diffuse."}
{"trans": "Long shall I remember the day we parted,  \nIn the tower we saw in view  \nThe moonbeams blend with water like a stream."}
{"trans": "At night when winds abate and I'm going home, the moon has brightened the river like a glass of jade."}
{"trans": "Dreams break off by native hills and rills, Shut off by endless streams and misty hills."}
{"trans": "The love-knot's woven in vain from ribbon fine, \nWhile on the riverhead rises the tide benign."}
{"trans": "Gazing afar over the waves stretching for thousands of miles, the evening mist hangs thick over the vast southern skies."}
{"trans": "With tears I ask the flowers, but they fail to bring an answer;\nI see red blooms fly over the swing again."}
{"trans": "Alone stand I when fallen flowers are whirling down; together fly a pair of swallows in the misty rain."}
{"trans": "A lonely grave a thousand miles away, nowhere to pour out my misery."}
{"trans": "Day after day of longing for you unseen, yet drinking water from the same river."}
{"trans": "Though vows remain, brocade messages are hard to send."}
{"trans": "The old tales of the Six Dynasties are gone with the flowing water, leaving only the cold mist and withered grass frozen in green."}
{"trans": "With a feather fan and a silken hood, I talk and laugh  \nWhile the foe's ships are destroyed, swallowed by the flames."}
{"trans": "In the night, hearing several crane calls, all say the royal army will soon arrive."}
{"trans": "To have a son one should be like Sun Zhongmou!"}
{"trans": "Thirty years of achievement are but dust and cloud, Eight thousand miles are but clouds and the moon."}
{"trans": "Under the Buddha Li Shrine, crows and sacrificial drums echo all around."}
{"trans": "Drunk, I lean on my sword in western breeze; \nI feel the river waves still boost my will."}
{"trans": "The river rushes like a whale, the mountains stand like a crouching tiger, such natural peril is no human design."}
{"trans": "The mist shrouds the tower, the moonlight bewilders the ferry."}
{"trans": "The bright flute plays in sunlight; at night Fishermen's songs float far wide; Old men fish merrily, Maidens pick lotus with pride."}
{"trans": "Amid the fragrance of the rice flowers, talk of a good year, with frogs croaking everywhere."}
{"trans": "A hundred years of ups and downs, we part in woe;\nWhile the moon we saw still shines on us below."}
{"trans": "Helplessly the blossoms fall; as if with deep regret swallows return."}
{"trans": "Orchid buds at the foot of the hill: short streams imbibe;\nThe sandy path amidst the pines: unstained by mud;\nDrizzling is the evening rain with cuckoos' songs imbued."}
{"trans": "Amid the drizzle falls the rustling of parasol trees, Murmuring, drop on drop, at dusk."}
{"trans": "Swallows fly here and there,  \nInquiring where is spring, alas!  \nIn the pool alone green grass grows."}
{"trans": "I long to ride the wind and return there, yet fear those marble towers and jade rooftops are too high and cold for me."}
{"trans": "Like a golden dream passes away, I turn my head with tears all o’ver my face."}
{"trans": "a thousand miles clear autumn in Southern sky, the river flows along with skies boundless autumn dye."}
{"trans": "Red berries grow in southern land. In spring, how many load the trees?"}
{"trans": "The west is veiled in rain, the east basks in sunshine. My gallant is as deep in love as the day is fine."}
{"trans": "At the Pavilion of Farewell, the scenery arouses my sorrow ever more."}
{"trans": "Outshining all in the three kingdoms' strife,  \nYou won your fame by the Stone Fortress Array."}
{"trans": "Gather your rosebuds while you may, Old Time is still a-flying."}
{"trans": "Infinite good is the sunset glow, But oh! 'tis near dying day."}
{"trans": "The moon like a golden bow and drop dew like pearls: this is a night in September."}
{"trans": "Gathering nectar from flowers, to whom do you bring sweetness? For whom with toil is honey made?"}
{"trans": "Widespread yellow clouds suffuse the dying day,\n\nThe north wind blows the snow and wild geese away."}
{"trans": "The sudden rain from the front mountains crosses the stream, washing away all the summer heat."}
